---
description: >-
  Layout and naming for feature pipeline markdown under features/.
  Apply when editing specification, HANDOFF, critic reports, or QA docs.
globs: "features/**/*.md"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Feature artifacts

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|--------|
| Type | Rule |
| Audience | Specialists writing `features/{slug}/` markdown |
| Adapt | Do not add a product name. Artifact names stay pack-owned. |

- One folder per request: `features/{kebab-slug}/`. Reuse it; do not fork a second spec for the same ask.
- **route.md** is required before specialists (`change_class` micro | minor | feature).
- Feature class: `pipeline-state.json`, `prd.md`, `state/{agent}.json`, `decisions.md`, `signoff-requirements.md`, optional `architecture.md` / `implementation-plan.md` / `architect-concerns.md` / `signoff-architect.md`, `signoff-ba.md`, `spec-order.md`, `test-plan.md`, child folders `features/{slug}/{child}/specification.md`, telemetry/dev HANDOFFs per child, parent `qa-test-cases.md`, `qa-signoff.md`, `RETRO.md`.
- Micro/minor: `patch.md` plus skipped-step stubs per change-routing; still `deploy-result.env` and `RETRO.md` after devops. Flat folder (no PM, no children).
- Fill every spec section (`N/A — reason` if needed). Label assumptions. Every Must FR needs an AC.
- HANDOFF `status` is `SUCCESS` | `BLOCKED` | `BLOCKED_CHALLENGE_PM` | `ASSUMPTIONS_USED` | `FAILED` as defined by the agent brief. Never `SUCCESS` with blocking open questions.
- Planning sign-off files use `SIGNOFF: approved`. Parent writes them; specialists do not.
- Critic verdicts: `approve` | `approve-with-nits` | `changes-required`. Findings cite FR/AC/section or file path.
- Do not put product source under `features/`. Do not treat `assets/example-specification.md` as a live feature spec.
